# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 14. SMTP & Email (Transactional Emails — OTP, Welcome, etc.)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# SMTP settings can be configured directly in the Communicator UI via:
#   POST /api/v1/smtp  (create SMTP configuration)
#   PUT  /api/v1/smtp/{id}  (update)
#   POST /api/v1/smtp/{id}/test  (test connection)
#
# Email templates are managed via:
#   GET  /api/v1/email-templates  (list all templates)
#   POST /api/v1/email-templates  (create a new template)
#   PUT  /api/v1/email-templates/{id}  (update)
#   POST /api/v1/email/send  (send a templated email)
#   GET  /api/v1/email/logs  (view send history)
#
# Default templates are seeded on first run:
#   - "OTP Verification" (category: otp)
#     Variables: {{code}}, {{name}}, {{expiry_minutes}}, {{year}}, {{brand_name}}
#   - "Welcome Email" (category: welcome)
#     Variables: {{name}}, {{brand_name}}, {{dashboard_url}}, {{year}}
#   - "Password Reset" (category: password_reset)
#     Variables: {{name}}, {{brand_name}}, {{reset_url}}, {{expiry_minutes}}, {{year}}
#   - "Order Confirmation" (category: order)
#     Variables: {{name}}, {{brand_name}}, {{order_number}}, {{order_total}}, {{order_date}}, {{year}}
#
# Example SMTP configurations:
#
# Gmail:
#   Host: smtp.gmail.com
#   Port: 587
#   Security: starttls
#   Auth: login
#   Username: your@gmail.com
#   Password: your-app-password  (use App Passwords, not your regular password)
#
# Outlook/Office 365:
#   Host: smtp.office365.com
#   Port: 587
#   Security: starttls
#   Auth: login
#
# SendGrid:
#   Host: smtp.sendgrid.net
#   Port: 587
#   Security: starttls
#   Auth: plain
#   Username: apikey
#   Password: your-sendgrid-api-key
#
# Amazon SES:
#   Host: email-smtp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
#   Port: 587
#   Security: starttls
#   Auth: login
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 15. OTP Engine Security (Banking-Grade)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTP_SESSION_SECRET is used to sign short-lived session tokens issued after
# successful OTP verification. Change this to a random 32+ character string
# in production. The session token prevents replay attacks — the client must
# present it for the next step (e.g., completing sign-up).
#
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
OTP_SESSION_SECRET=
#
# Banking-grade security features enabled:
#   - 12-char alphanumeric OTP with rejection sampling (no modulo bias)
#   - HMAC-SHA256 hash storage (plaintext NEVER in database)
#   - IP/device binding (verification rejected if IP changes)
#   - Per-recipient AND per-IP rate limiting (prevents SMS bombing)
#   - Replay attack protection (session token on verification)
#   - In-app messages store masked OTP only (A7x••••••9mK)
#   - Full audit logging with IP addresses
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 16. nID Tenant Sync (Real-Time Tenant Management)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connects the Communicator to nID's tenant system for real-time sync.
# When a tenant is created/updated in nID, the Communicator receives
# a webhook and keeps its tenant mirror in sync.
#
# PLATFORM_ADMIN_SECRET: Shared secret for nID platform-admin operations
# (tenant creation, tenant management). Set this in nID's .env as well.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
PLATFORM_ADMIN_SECRET=
#
# NID_WEBHOOK_RECEIVE_SECRET: Secret for verifying incoming nID webhooks.
# This should match the webhookSecret generated when creating a tenant in nID.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
NID_WEBHOOK_RECEIVE_SECRET=
#
# nID Tenant Sync API endpoints:
#   POST /api/v1/nid/webhook              — Receive webhook from nID
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/tenants              — List all synced tenants
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/tenants/{id}         — Get tenant details
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/connection           — Get connection health
#   PUT  /api/v1/nid/connection           — Update connection settings
#   POST /api/v1/nid/redirect/create      — Start tenant creation redirect
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/redirect/callback    — Handle nID callback
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/redirect/{state}     — Check redirect status
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/sync-log             — View sync event log
#
# nID Dashboard endpoints (separate app at localhost:3001):
#   - Login as staff (phone + OTP) or platform admin (secret)
#   - Create Tenant button in sidebar
#   - Manage API keys, staff, settings
#   - View all tenants at /tenants
#
# Setup steps:
# 1. Set PLATFORM_ADMIN_SECRET in both nID and Communicator .env files
# 2. Run migration: psql -d communicator -f backend-rs/migrations/0058_nid_tenant_sync.sql
# 3. Configure connection: PUT /api/v1/nid/connection with nID base URL and secrets
# 4. Create tenant in nID dashboard → webhook auto-syncs to Communicator
# 5. Tenant appears in Communicator at GET /api/v1/nid/tenants
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 17. nID Organization Sync (Real-Time Organization Management)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connects the Communicator to nID's organization system for real-time sync.
# Organizations sit within tenants and represent verified business entities.
# When an organization is created/updated in nID, the Communicator receives
# a webhook and keeps its organization mirror in sync.
#
# Organization sync uses the same PLATFORM_ADMIN_SECRET and nID connection
# as tenant sync. No additional secrets needed.
#
# nID Organization Sync API endpoints:
#   POST /api/v1/nid/org/webhook              — Receive webhook from nID
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/org/organizations        — List all synced organizations
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/org/organizations/{id}   — Get organization details
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/org/connection           — Get connection settings
#   PUT  /api/v1/nid/org/connection           — Update connection settings
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/org/health               — Get connection health
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/org/sync-log             — View sync event log
#   POST /api/v1/nid/org/redirect/create      — Start org creation redirect
#   GET  /api/v1/nid/org/redirect/callback    — Handle nID callback
#
# nID Dashboard Organization Management:
#   - "Organizations" tab in sidebar (next to Overview)
#   - "+ Create Organization" button with form (legal name, registration, country)
#   - Member management: invite employees, view members table
#   - Verification status display (KYB badge)
#
# Communicator Organization Dashboard:
#   - Navigate to /organizations in the Communicator frontend
#   - View synced organizations with status badges
#   - "Create Organization" button redirects to nID for creation
#   - Connection settings and health monitoring
#   - Step-by-step guide for the flow
#
# Work Profile (nID profile-ui):
#   - "Work" tab shows both tenant AND organization memberships
#   - Organizations section shows legal name, country, role, admin status
#
# Setup steps:
# 1. Run migration: psql -d communicator -f backend-rs/migrations/0059_nid_organization_sync.sql
# 2. Configure connection via PUT /api/v1/nid/org/connection (or use defaults)
# 3. Create organization in nID dashboard → webhook auto-syncs to Communicator
# 4. Organization appears in Communicator at GET /api/v1/nid/org/organizations
# 5. Profile updates in nID sync to Communicator in real-time (<1 second)
#
